===== B7. RustSec — advisory pages, with a positive control =====
https://rustsec.org/packages/rust-cache  .html -> HTTP 404
https://rustsec.org/packages/sccache     .html -> HTTP 404
https://rustsec.org/packages/atty        .html -> HTTP 200
https://rustsec.org/packages/serde       .html -> HTTP 404
atty carries a known advisory and returns 200, which is the positive
control proving a 404 is an absence of advisory rather than a broken
lookup. rust-cache 404s because it is an Action and has no crates.io
package at all, so gate 3 is inapplicable to it, not passed by it.

